Count Pairs Divisible By K

Explanation:

In this we need to count pairs where sum of the numbers is divisble by k;
so instead of summign2 numbers and then checking if remainder is 0, and doing complex stuff within the hashmap, 
we check if there is a complement in the hashmap for a particular remainder
if a remainder is existing alreeady in hashmap, we check if its complement is also exisitng.

here in hashmap we store remainder and its frequency instead of array numbers

Code:
class Solution {
    public int countKdivPairs(int[] arr, int k) {
        // code here
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        int count=0;
        
        for(int num:arr){
            int rem = num%k;
            int complement = (k-rem)%k;
            
            count+=map.getOrDefault(complement,0);
            
            map.put(rem,map.getOrDefault(rem,0)+1);
        }
        
        return count;
    }
}
